---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy | Nodex" description="What the Nodex website and apps collect.">
  <div class="flex min-h-screen flex-col">
    <main class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-3xl flex-1 flex-col px-6 py-12 sm:px-10">
      <a href="/" class="mb-10 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm opacity-60 hover:opacity-100">← Back to Nodex</a>

      <article class="py-7">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.045em]">Privacy</h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm opacity-50">Last updated: November 7, 2026</p>

        <div class="mt-8 space-y-7 text-[15px] leading-7 [&_h2]:mb-2 [&_h2]:text-lg [&_h2]:font-medium [&_h2]:tracking-tight [&_p]:opacity-70">
          <section>
            <h2>What this site collects</h2>
            <p>
              The Nodex website counts page views and clicks on download buttons, using Statsig. It
              sets no cookies and stores nothing in your browser, so one visit cannot be connected
              to another. It does not record what you read, and it stops counting when your browser
              sends a Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal. There is no advertising and no
              account creation.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Download and outbound links</h2>
            <p>
              When you click download or repository links, you leave this site and go to
              third-party services such as GitHub, Homebrew and Apple's TestFlight. Those services may collect network
              logs, browser metadata, and any information you choose to provide there.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Hosting</h2>
            <p>
              This site is served by GitHub Pages behind Cloudflare, which keep their own network
              logs. Nodex reads daily totals of update-check requests from Cloudflare, not
              individual visitors.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Usage analytics in the desktop app</h2>
            <p>
              The app sends anonymous usage analytics to Statsig so we can tell how many people use
              Nodex and which parts work. It is on by default, says so on first launch, and sends
              nothing until you have had time to turn it off. Turn it off any time in Settings →
              General → Privacy, or set <code>DO_NOT_TRACK=1</code>. Turning it off discards
              anything not yet sent.
            </p>
            <p>
              Each event carries a random ID that is created on your computer and is not connected
              to your account, plus the app version, release channel, operating system, processor
              type and language. Events say that something happened: a launch, a conversation
              started, which Agent and public model it used, how a turn ended and how many tokens
              it used, how long it took. Prompts, responses, code, titles, file names and paths are
              never sent, and a model you configured privately is reported only as &ldquo;other&rdquo;.
              Statsig receives your IP address as any web service does and uses it to derive a
              country. Settings shows exactly what has been sent.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Crash reports in the desktop app</h2>
            <p>
              Crash reports go to Sentry so we can fix failures. They are on by default and are
              scrubbed on your computer first: prompts, transcripts, card text, local paths,
              credentials and request bodies are removed. Turn them off in Settings → General →
              Privacy. Session Replay is a separate setting that stays off unless you enable it, and
              it masks all text and inputs when you do.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Nodex Mobile</h2>
            <p>
              Nodex Mobile connects directly to Nodex on your computer over your local network or
              Tailscale, encrypted end to end, with no server of ours in between. It sends no usage
              analytics or crash reports. Your phone keeps its device credentials, messages not yet delivered,
              drafts and a copy of what it last showed you.
            </p>
            <p>
              On iPhone, if you turn notifications on, the computer running that Space encrypts each one
              for your phone before sending it. Our relay and Apple deliver it without being able to read
              it. They receive your device's notification token to route it, and the relay stores
              neither the token nor the notification.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Your content</h2>
            <p>
              Nodex stores your Pages and conversations on your computer. Analytics and crash
              reports do not include them. Agents you use send your messages to the provider you
              chose, under that provider's terms.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2>Contact and updates</h2>
            <p>
              If the privacy posture of the site changes, this page will be updated alongside the
              source in the public repository.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </article>
    </main>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
